WEBVTT

00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:02.130
Thank you.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.490
He doesn't hurt bad. Jim, you better get up there and take care of him.

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:52.620
Back to the past!

00:03:37.930 --> 00:03:38.810
It's the end of Carson.

00:03:39.260 --> 00:03:39.540
Yeah.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:43.110
Now we can join up with the mystery writers.

00:03:43.500 --> 00:03:44.160
Nothing to him.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.150
Can't tell who might get why.

00:03:47.110 --> 00:03:48.950
We'll follow them to the hideout.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:04.040
Are you hurt bad?

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:08.460
No, but I thought I'd wake up in the happy hunting grounds.

00:04:08.860 --> 00:04:11.420
Are they still there?

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:13.440
No, they've ridden away.

00:04:14.710 --> 00:04:15.890
Thought we were killed, I guess.

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.720
Looks like we might be able to get up over there.

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:35.750
Are you all right, kid?

00:04:36.570 --> 00:04:37.630
Sure is all right.

00:04:37.940 --> 00:04:39.660
Take a wilder horse not to hurt him.

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:40.800
That's the spirit.

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.120
They leave a broad trail. It'll be easy to follow them.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.970
Yes, but not too easy to get Johnny away from them.

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:12.970
They think she's a boy, and that may help us a bit.

00:05:13.720 --> 00:05:14.980
Come, let's get our horses.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.350
Hey, Steve, boss here yet?

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:38.280
Yeah, he's waiting for you.

00:05:39.230 --> 00:05:41.030
What are you men doing here without your uniform?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.310
Oh, we have a little business in town.

00:05:43.670 --> 00:05:44.010
Uh-oh.

00:06:09.630 --> 00:06:12.600
Say, boss, the lucky thing you had us follow the riders.

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.770
Carson was trailing them.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:17.280
Carson? Find out anything?

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.000
No, he's dead.

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:20.370
Are you sure?

00:06:21.260 --> 00:06:21.620
Absolutely.

00:06:22.690 --> 00:06:25.010
We caught him between us and the riders, and he went over a cliff.

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:25.630
Good.

00:06:26.600 --> 00:06:27.520
Where's my good boy?

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:29.960
The boys have got him right outside the door.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:36.490
It was pretty smart the way you had the mystery writers come right into town and get him. Yeah

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:40.770
No one will ever suspect now that I'm their leader. Hey

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.300
Well, now to make Fargo talk

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:02.410
Ready to tell me why you hit that gold shipment?

00:07:04.080 --> 00:07:08.820
That gold belongs to the United States government, and I'm not going to let you steal it.

00:07:09.270 --> 00:07:12.970
You can kill me, but I won't tell you where it is.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:16.980
No? Not even if it means the life of your son?

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.780
Son? I've got no son.

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:21.380
Aren't you?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.880
You can't bluff me, Fargo.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:27.050
Bring in the boy.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:39.600
I don't know you. I got no son.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:44.580
There's a trick to try to make me tell where the gold is, but it won't work.

00:07:46.090 --> 00:07:47.970
Do you know me? I'm Johnny.

00:07:50.120 --> 00:07:53.400
I don't know what your game is, but you'll get nothing out of me.

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:59.140
There's only one man I'll tell where I hid that gold, and that's Kit Carson.

00:08:00.348 --> 00:08:02.048
He was in charge of that pack train.

00:08:02.684 --> 00:08:04.104
And he's got a right to know.

00:08:20.124 --> 00:08:20.324
Joy.

00:08:20.476 --> 00:08:21.836
not your son, Fargo.

00:08:22.812 --> 00:08:24.032
Well, he must be a spy.

00:08:24.988 --> 00:08:27.448
Eh, he's found out too much about us to let him go now.

00:08:29.212 --> 00:08:29.712
Oh wait!

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:38.030
what's the matter Fargo oh yeah you're not gonna hurt that boy why should you

00:08:38.030 --> 00:08:42.500
care he's not your son he's found out too much about it anyway we got to shut

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:42.920
his mouth

00:09:00.284 --> 00:09:01.464
Please bring him back.

00:09:03.484 --> 00:09:04.824
Tell him to bring the boy back.

00:09:05.660 --> 00:09:06.280
Bring it back.

00:09:07.868 --> 00:09:09.748
I'll take the only chances on you double-crossing us.

00:09:10.204 --> 00:09:10.704
Fargo.

00:09:11.708 --> 00:09:13.188
We're keeping your boy here.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:15.120
Until you've just where the gold is.

00:09:31.436 --> 00:09:32.516
Girl is not with them.

00:09:33.228 --> 00:09:35.808
Now is our chance to get her out of there before they get back.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.480
The entrance is well guarded.

00:09:37.708 --> 00:09:39.108
We'll have to find another way in.

00:10:51.280 --> 00:10:51.560
Let's go!

00:11:20.412 --> 00:11:22.412
That must be where they have Johnny.

00:11:22.652 --> 00:11:24.692
There where the man with the rifle is standing guard.

00:12:02.260 --> 00:12:06.580
Sure smells good.

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.870
Nothing like a good buffalo steak.

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:13.560
You burn that, I'll scuff you alive.

00:12:19.040 --> 00:12:20.200
Ain't that grab ready yet?

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.210
Someone get it or I'll throw it away!

00:12:34.730 --> 00:12:35.930
One of these is for the kids.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.210
Now, don't make any mistake and eat them both yourself.

00:14:01.180 --> 00:14:29.920
Hey, look at Jake file into that buffalo meat don't blame him it sure good

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.490
How long has this meat been a hunk?

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:33.810
What do you care?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:34.790
Taste good, don't it?

00:14:47.400 --> 00:14:48.000
Hey, Jake!

00:14:48.750 --> 00:14:49.510
Want another hunk?

00:14:57.660 --> 00:14:59.700
Jake ain't up to his usual form today.

00:15:06.270 --> 00:15:10.480
They said they'd kill me if Daddy didn't show them where he hid the gold.

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:14.900
And as soon as he does tell them, they'll kill him.

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:18.450
He mustn't tell them. Please don't let him tell.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:22.390
The only way that we can stop him now is to show him that you're safe.

00:15:26.510 --> 00:15:29.980
Well, I suppose I've got to release Sandy so he can...

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:38.030
come and eat. There's one of them coming.

00:15:51.900 --> 00:15:53.680
What things happened to Jake?

00:16:00.120 --> 00:16:01.080
What's the matter? Is he sick?

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.710
No, he's been knocked cold.

00:16:02.850 --> 00:16:03.590
That can't be.

00:16:03.810 --> 00:16:05.690
He was right where we could see him all the time.

00:16:05.830 --> 00:16:08.250
Well, just the same, I'm going to make sure everything's all right.

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.700
You men look after Jake.

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:19.480
I've got to let him in, or he'll suspect and call the others.

00:16:20.140 --> 00:16:21.460
You act like you're still a prisoner.

00:16:28.560 --> 00:16:29.560
Everything all right, Sandy?

00:16:32.760 --> 00:16:45.280
Come on down the door.

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:37.360
Thank you very much.

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:01.930
Thank you.
